---
description: When the user message is just "git", commit and push
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user sends a message that is essentially just **git** (optionally with minor punctuation), treat it as an explicit request to **commit all current project changes and push to origin**, without asking for confirmation.

Follow the safe git protocol: status/diff/log, clear message, no secrets, no `--no-verify`, no force push to main, never update git config.
